# Required in production; local dev falls back to Shopify's sample profile (see
# docs/getting-started.md#agent-profile) — public URL of your UCP agent profile
#
# The profile MUST be served with Content-Type: application/json. Shopify's fetcher
# rejects text/plain (verified 2026-07-04 — a GitHub gist raw URL fails with
# "profile_malformed: Invalid content type"). Host it somewhere that sets the JSON
# content-type: your own deploy (apps/web serves /agent-profile.json), a CDN, or an
# object store. The self-authored sample lives at profile/agent-profile.json for reference,
# but is NOT usable as AGENT_PROFILE_URL unless you host it with the correct content-type.
#
# The value below is Shopify's published sample profile (application/json, verified
# working keyless 2026-07-04). Fine for local dev; publish your own identity before prod.
AGENT_PROFILE_URL=https://shopify.dev/ucp/agent-profiles/2026-04-08/valid-with-capabilities.json

# Optional — raises rate limits. Leave empty for keyless anonymous access (works fine for dev).
# Create at Shopify Dev Dashboard → Catalog. Never expose to the browser.
SHOPIFY_CATALOG_CLIENT_ID=
SHOPIFY_CATALOG_CLIENT_SECRET=
